cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Keystone, please cite it.
title: "Keystone: a clinical decision-evidence benchmark for chat assistants and their rubrics"
abstract: >-
  Keystone pairs every source clinical conversation with twins that change exactly one fact and with a
  paraphrase-only control, annotates each source with the decision it asks for and each twin with the
  evidence state that follows, and scores both the assistant's action and the applicability of the
  physician rubric that grades it. Built on HealthBench (OpenAI, MIT).
type: dataset
version: "0.4.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xinxuxin/keystone-bench"
